  "output": "Here's the performance analysis with actionable fixes:\n\n---\n\n## Performance Analysis: HR Policy Bot\n\n### 1. N+1 Query Patterns\n\n**`src/api/routes.py:125,138,180` — New DB connection per request (CRITICAL)**\n\nEach endpoint opens a fresh connection rather than using a shared instance:\n```python\n# Current (broken)\n@router.get(\"/queries\")\nasync def list_queries(...):\n    db = DatabaseManager()  # new connection every call\n    return await db.list_queries(limit=limit)\n\n# Fix: inject a singleton via dependency\n_db = DatabaseManager()\n\nasync def get_db() -> DatabaseManager:\n    return _db\n\n@router.get(\"/queries\")\nasync def list_queries(db: DatabaseManager = Depends(get_db)):\n    return await db.list_queries(limit=limit)\n```\n\n**`src/api/routes.py:144-147` — 3 round-trips for one record**\n```python\n# Current: 3 separate queries\nagent_responses = await db.get_agent_responses(query_id)\norchestrator_response = await db.get_orchestrator_response(query_id)\nfeedback = await db.get_feedback_for_query(query_id)\n\n# Fix: run concurrently\nagent_responses, orchestrator_response, feedback = await asyncio.gather(\n    db.get_agent_responses(query_id),\n    db.get_orchestrator_response(query_id),\n    db.get_feedback_for_query(query_id),\n)\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. Caching Opportunities\n\n**`src/agents/specialist.py:73-75` — `policy_registry.json` read 8 times at startup**\n```python\n# Current: each specialist reads the file independently\ndef _load_instruments(self, agent_id: str) -> list[dict]:\n    with open(_REGISTRY_PATH) as f:\n        registry = json.load(f)   # file I/O 8 times\n    return [r for r in registry if agent_id in r[\"agent_ids\"]]\n\n# Fix: load once at module level\nwith open(_REGISTRY_PATH) as f:\n    _REGISTRY: list[dict] = json.load(f)\n\ndef _load_instruments(self, agent_id: str) -> list[dict]:\n    return [r for r in _REGISTRY if agent_id in r[\"agent_ids\"]]\n```\n\n**`src/fetch/engine.py:69-74` — regex recompiled on every URL**\n```python\n# Current\ndef _normalize_url(self, url: str) -> str:\n    import re\n    if re.search(r'laws-lois\\.justice\\.gc\\.ca/eng/acts/[^/]+/$', url):\n        ...\n\n# Fix: compile at class level\n_LAWS_URL_RE = re.compile(r'laws-lois\\.justice\\.gc\\.ca/eng/acts/[^/]+/$')\n\ndef _normalize_url(self, url: str) -> str:\n    if self._LAWS_URL_RE.search(url):\n        ...\n```\n\n**`src/llm/client.py` — `GenerativeModel` recreated on every `chat()` call**\n\nCache model instances by name:\n```python\n_model_cache: dict[str, genai.GenerativeModel] = {}\n\ndef _make_model(self, model: str | None) -> genai.GenerativeModel:\n    key = model or self._default_model\n    if key not in _model_cache:\n        _model_cache[key] = genai.GenerativeModel(key)\n    return _model_cache[key]\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. Memory Leaks\n\n**`src/api/websocket.py:33-46` — stale connections never pruned (CRITICAL)**\n```python\n# Current: dead connections accumulate if client crashes\nasync def disconnect(self, query_id: str) -> None:\n    if query_id in self._connections:\n        del self._connections[query_id]\n\n# Fix: wrap sends in try/except and prune on failure\nasync def send(self, query_id: str, data: dict) -> None:\n    ws = self._connections.get(query_id)\n    if ws:\n        try:\n            await ws.send_json(data)\n        except Exception:\n            del self._connections[query_id]  # prune dead connection\n```\n\n**`src/fetch/engine.py:45-48` — domain semaphores grow unbounded**\n```python\n# Fix: bound the dict with an LRU or prune stale entries\nfrom functools import lru_cache\n\n# Or cap with a max-size defaultdict using collections.OrderedDict\n_MAX_TRACKED_DOMAINS = 200\n\ndef _get_semaphore(self, domain: str) -> asyncio.Semaphore:\n    if domain not in self._domain_semaphores:\n        if len(self._domain_semaphores) >= _MAX_TRACKED_DOMAINS:\n            # evict oldest\n            self._domain_semaphores.pop(next(iter(self._domain_semaphores)))\n        self._domain_semaphores[domain] = asyncio.Semaphore(3)\n    return self._domain_semaphores[domain]\n```\n\n---\n\n### 4. Database / SQL\n\n**`src/data/db.py:312-319` — per-row TTL calculation in SQL**\n```sql\n-- Current: datetime() runs for every row examined\nSELECT * FROM fetch_cache\nWHERE url = ?\n  AND datetime(fetched_at, '+' || ttl_hours || ' hours') > datetime('now')\n\n-- Fix: add an expires_at column computed at insert time\n-- Migration:\nALTER TABLE fetch_cache ADD COLUMN expires_at TEXT;\nUPDATE fetch_cache SET expires_at = datetime(fetched_at, '+' || ttl_hours || ' hours');\nCREATE INDEX idx_fetch_cache_expires ON fetch_cache(url, expires_at);\n\n-- New query (indexed, no per-row function call):\nSELECT * FROM fetch_cache WHERE url = ? AND expires_at > datetime('now')\n```\n\n---\n\n### 5. Frontend Memory Leak\n\n**`static/js/app.js:391-401` — event listeners stack up across queries**\n```javascript\n// Current: new listeners added every time feedback is shown\ndocument.querySelectorAll('.feedback-buttons .btn-feedback').forEach(btn => {\n    btn.addEventListener('click', () => { ... });\n});\n\n// Fix: wire once at init, or use event delegation\ndocument.querySelector('.feedback-buttons').addEventListener('click', (e) => {\n    const btn = e.target.closest('.btn-feedback');\n    if (!btn) return;\n    handleFeedback(btn.dataset.value);\n});\n```\n\n**`static/js/app.js:145` — DOM query inside hot agent-status loop**\n```javascript\n// Current: querySelector on every status update\nconst agentItem = agentList.querySelector(`[data-agent=\"${data.agent_id}\"]`);\n\n// Fix: cache references when agents are first rendered\nconst _agentElements = new Map();\n\nfunction registerAgentElement(agentId, el) {\n    _agentElements.set(agentId, el);\n}\n\nfunction handleAgentStatusUpdate(data) {\n    const agentItem = _agentElements.get(data.agent_id); // O(1) map lookup\n    ...\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### Priority Order\n\n| Priority | Fix | Expected Impact |\n|----------|-----|----------------|\n| 1 | Shared DB connection singleton | Eliminates connection-per-request overhead |\n| 2 | `asyncio.gather` for query detail | ~3x faster query detail endpoint |\n| 3 | Load registry once | Eliminates 7 redundant file reads at startup |\n| 4 | Prune stale WebSocket connections | Prevents memory growth under load |\n| 5 | Pre-computed `expires_at` + index | Faster cache lookups at scale |\n| 6 | Pre-compile regex | Small CPU win on bulk fetches |\n| 7 | Frontend event delegation | Prevents JS listener leak across sessions |\n\nThe two highest-leverage fixes are the **DB connection singleton** (items 1–2) and the **WebSocket leak** (item 4) — those are the only ones that compound negatively over time.\n",
